      "body": "## Overview\n\nThis PR started as a fix: with `--reasoning-parser hf`, `ResponseTemplateParser` inherited `Parser.count_reasoning_tokens`, which returns 0, so usage reported `completion_tokens_details.reasoning_tokens: 0` while returning the reasoning text.\n\n#62052 has since replaced `ResponseTemplateParser.count_reasoning_tokens` with its own implementation, which fixes that. After rebasing, I dropped my implementation in favour of the one on main and kept only the unit tests, which `tests/parser/test_response_template.py` didn't have for this method.\n\n## What the tests pin\n\n`test_count_reasoning_tokens_counts_thinking_content`, with the Gemma 4 response template:\n\n| case | output | expected |\n|---|---|---|\n| closed | thinking region opened and closed in the output | 2 |\n| opened_by_prompt | the prompt opens the thinking region | 3 |\n| unclosed | the output ends inside the thinking region | 3 |\n| no_thinking | no thinking region | 0 |\n\nDelimiters are not counted.\n\n## Validation\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/parser/test_response_template.py -q\n# 74 passed\n```\n\nThe four cases pass on main as of #62052 and fail on the code before it (`assert 0 == 2`, `assert 0 == 3`, `assert 0 == 3`). `pre-commit run` passes on the changed file (ruff, mypy, typos, test tethering).\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\nAI assistance (Claude Code) was used to write this change and run the validation above.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
